          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 9,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "Her house — For the reception of her guests. Seven - Many pillars; whereby is intimated the beauty and stability of the church. Pillars - Prophets, and apostles, and ministers."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 9,
              "v_start": 2,
              "v_end": 2,
              "text": "Killed — Made provision for the guests. Mingled - With water, as they used to do in those hot countries. Furnished - With all necessaries, and now waits for the guests."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 9,
              "v_start": 3,
              "v_end": 3,
              "text": "Maidens — Her servants to invite the guests, ministers of the word whom he calls maidens for the decency of the parable; for wisdom being compared to a great princess, was fit to be attended upon by maidens. Highest places - From such high seats as those from which Judges delivered their sentences, and officers made proclamations."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 9,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "Simple — Ignorant, and weak."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "psalm",
          "ref": "Psalm 34:9-14",
          "refKey": "Ps.34.9-Ps.34.14",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "faith-and-trust",
              "peace-of-god",
              "providence-and-care",
              "wisdom"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "exhortation",
              "trust"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 34,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "Fear — Reverence, serve, and trust him: for fear is commonly put for all the parts of God's worship."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 34,
              "v_start": 12,
              "v_end": 12,
              "text": "Life — A long and happy life, begun in this world and continued forever in the next. Good - In which he may enjoy good, prosperity or happiness."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 34,
              "v_start": 13,
              "v_end": 13,
              "text": "Evil — From all manner of evil speaking, from all injurious, false and deceitful speeches."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 34,
              "v_start": 14,
              "v_end": 14,
              "text": "Depart — From all sin. Do good - Be ready to perform all good offices to all men. Seek - Study by all means possible to live peaceable with all men. Pursue it - Do not only embrace it gladly when it is offered, but follow hard after it, when it seems to flee away from thee."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "second",
          "ref": "Ephesians 5:15-20",
