              "v_start": 15,
              "v_end": 15,
              "text": "Circumspectly — Exactly, with the utmost accuracy, getting to the highest pitch of every point of holiness. Not as fools - Who think not where they are going, or do not make the best of their way."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 16,
              "v_end": 16,
              "text": "With all possible care redeeming the time — Saving all you can for the best purposes; buying every possible moment out of the hands of sin and Satan; out of the hands of sloth, ease, pleasure, worldly business; the more diligently, because the present are evil days, days of the grossest ignorance, immorality, and profaneness."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 17,
              "v_end": 17,
              "text": "What the will of the Lord is — In every time, place, and circumstance."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 18,
              "v_end": 18,
              "text": "Wherein is excess — That is, which leads to debauchery of every kind. But be ye filled with the Spirit - In all his graces, who gives a more noble pleasure than wine can do."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 19,
              "v_end": 19,
              "text": "Speaking to each other — By the Spirit. In the Psalms - Of David. And hymns - Of praise. And spiritual songs - On any divine subject. By there being no inspired songs, peculiarly adapted to the Christian dispensation, as there were to the Jewish, it is evident that the promise of the Holy Ghost to believers, in the last days, was by his larger effusion to supply the lack of it. Singing with your hearts - As well as your voice. To the Lord - Jesus, who searcheth the heart."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 5,
              "v_start": 20,
              "v_end": 20,
              "text": "Giving thanks — At all times and places. And for all things - Prosperous or adverse, since all work together for good. In the name of, or through, our Lord Jesus Christ - By whom we receive all good things."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "gospel",
          "ref": "John 6:51-58",
          "refKey": "John.6.51-John.6.58",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "atonement",
              "incarnation",
              "resurrection-and-life"
            ],
            "image": [
              "blood",
              "bread"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "assurance",
              "wonder-and-awe"
            ],
            "function": [
              "table-communion"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 51,
              "v_end": 51,
              "text": "If any eat of this bread — That is, believe in me: he shall live forever - In other words, he that believeth to the end shall be saved. My flesh which I will give you - This whole discourse concerning his flesh and blood refers directly to his passion, and but remotely, if at all, to the Lord's Supper."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 52,
              "v_end": 52,
              "text": "Observe the degrees: the Jews are tried here; the disciples, ver. 60-66, the apostles, ver. 67."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 53,
              "v_end": 53,
              "text": "Unless ye eat the flesh of the Son of man — Spiritually: unless ye draw continual virtue from him by faith. Eating his flesh is only another expression for believing."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 55,
              "v_end": 55,
              "text": "Meat — drink indeed - With which the soul of a believer is as truly fed, as his body with meat and drink."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 57,
              "v_end": 57,
              "text": "I live by the Father — Being one with him. He shall live by me -Being one with me. Amazing union!"
            },
            {
              "chapter": 6,
              "v_start": 58,
              "v_end": 58,
              "text": "This is — That is, I am the bread - Which is not like the manna your fathers ate, who died notwithstanding."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
